        {
            "id": "ar_note_1",
            "text": "**Audio distorts a shape** The hexagon is the **source**, noise is the **map**, and the audio envelope drives the **amount** of distortion.",
            "x": 1035.3925,
            "y": 138.19139,
            "width": 228.76575,
            "height": 102.91884,
            "color": 0
        },
        {
            "id": "ar_note_2",
            "text": "**Noise as a map, not a background.** Bright pixels in the noise push source pixels further. When audio is silent, amount=0 and the hexagon is crisp.",
            "x": -122.94783,
            "y": 655.1078,
            "width": 300.0,
            "height": 100.0,
            "color": 3
        },
        {
            "id": "ar_note_3",
            "text": "**Audio → visual bridge.** The Gain's **rms** output is a smoothed audio envelope. The wire remap scales 0.0–0.5 RMS into 0.0–0.6 displacement amount.",
            "x": 661.5213,
            "y": 174.64781,
